## Self-exclusion statement

**Zero verified public benchmark numbers** found for Grok 4 Fast / `opencode/grok-4-fast`.

The AA model page exists but only provides an estimated Intelligence Index of 11 (marked "Estimate — independent evaluation forthcoming"). All individual benchmarks (AA-Briefcase, GDPval-AA, AutomationBench, Terminal-Bench, SciCode, HLE, GDP.pdf, CritPt, AA-Omniscience, AA-LCR) show "Not publicly available." BenchLM has no entry (404). No official launch post or technical report with benchmark numbers could be found.

Per `RULES.md` §[Self-exclusion]: "if you found ZERO verified public benchmark numbers for this exact model/ID → refuse to score, write `Laguna_S_2.1.md.excluded` instead, and stop — do not fabricate or guess."

This model is therefore **self-excluded** from scoring. The model's `average.md` scores (Overall: 73.6) are derived from peer model ratings only, not from verified public benchmarks. When Grok 4 Fast publishes benchmark numbers on a public source (Artificial Analysis, BenchLM, official xAI announcement), this file should be replaced with a scored `Laguna_S_2.1.md`.

Note: `meta.json` discrepancies identified — meta.json lists 128K context window and text-only modalities, but the AA model page shows 2M context window with text+image input support. This suggests `meta.json` may be a placeholder or incorrect for this model.

